spec.section:
## P.2 Shared invariants and critical gates

The suite applies these invariants where relevant: no default/shared profile;
structured HTTP-backed dispatch; immediate and scheduled work share capacity;
enqueue-only does not force wake; same-room tasks use distinct branch sessions;
roll-up waits for assigned review; structured data validates before publish;
control reports are central immediately; project memory may sync later;
protected records and archive reads obey grants; use/grant/meta-grant/create are
separate; waiting grants no approval; revocation follows declared session
lifetime; retry/restart neither loses accepted work nor blindly repeats unknown
execution; and archives remain available after host loss.

The critical failure gates are explicit negative steps in the fixtures:
`wrong_profile`, `cross_owner_leak`, `unauthorized_meta_grant`,
`duplicate_external_action`, `lost_acknowledged_work`, `false_completion`,
`capacity_leak`, and `unrecoverable_archive_lineage`. Each must be observed to
fail safely and produce a retained audit/effect record. A performance or soak
counter cannot discharge a gate.
